<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<!-- Deploy wwwroot contents to the app's root, not _content/SpawnDev.WebTorrent/ -->
		<!-- Required for service worker scope — SW must be at app root to intercept all requests -->
		<StaticWebAssetBasePath Condition="$(StaticWebAssetBasePath) == ''">/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<Version>3.2.0</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v3.2.0 stable - first SpawnDev.WebTorrent minor cut since 3.1.0. Bundles five additive features on top of 3.1.7's wire-level seeder correctness fix; zero behavior change for consumers who don't opt in to any of the new surfaces. (1) Inbound TCP listener wired as a first-class API: `WebTorrentClientOptions.TcpListenPort` (null/0/&gt;0), `TcpListenAddress` (default `IPAddress.Any`), `WebTorrentClient.TcpListener` property + `EnsureTcpListenerAsync(port, address)` idempotent helper. Mainline clients (qBittorrent, libtorrent, Transmission, rqbit) can dial in by IP+port; listener peeks 68-byte BT handshake, routes by info_hash to the matching torrent. Full doc: `Docs/tcp-listener.md`. (2) Tracker advertising for the listener: opt-in `WebTorrentClientOptions.AdvertiseTcpListenerToTrackers` flag. When enabled, every HTTP / UDP tracker announce includes the listener's actual port in BEP 3 `port=` field so trackers put us in their compact peer list and mainline peers find us automatically (no manual `addPeers`). WebSocket tracker signaling is unaffected (WebRTC-only). (3) Pluggable piece-hash engine: new `IPieceHashEngine` interface + `SystemCryptoPieceHashEngine` default (System.Security.Cryptography). `WebTorrentClient.PieceHashEngine` property + `WebTorrentClientOptions.PieceHashEngine` slot-in let recheck-heavy workloads route through GPU / batched implementations without changing call sites. Default behavior (System.Security.Cryptography) is byte-identical to 3.1.x. (4) Bandwidth policy: new `BandwidthPolicy` enum (`Unlimited` / `Conservative` / `Metered` / `SeedingDisabled` / `Custom`) with translation through `WebTorrentClientOptions.BandwidthPolicy`. Conservative = 256 KiB/s upload ceiling, Metered = 64 KiB/s, SeedingDisabled = 0 (paused). Explicit `UploadLimit` always wins over the policy. Runtime knob: `WebTorrentClient.ApplyBandwidthPolicy(policy)`. (5) SipSorcery fork: `MediaStreamTrack.StreamStatus` setter widened from `internal` to `public` so consumers can flip direction post-construction without reflection or track recreation. Strict superset of upstream surface. New PlaywrightMultiTest coverage: 8 desktop tests across the five new surfaces. All shipped tests + interop matrix (qBittorrent live-swarm both directions, JS WebTorrent live-swarm via local SpawnDev.RTC tracker) green.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
		<Title>SpawnDev.WebTorrent</Title>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<Description>Pure C# BitTorrent/WebTorrent client. 18 BEPs including BEP 52 v2 (SHA-256 + Merkle + hybrid + pure-v2 end-to-end), real WebRTC P2P (browser + desktop via SpawnDev.RTC), DHT with mutable items (BEP 46 — AI agent communication), web seeds, media streaming with seeking via service worker, OPFS storage. Includes webtorrent-sw.js for COI headers + torrent streaming. No JavaScript dependencies. Runs on desktop (.NET + SIPSorcery) and browser (Blazor WASM + SpawnDev.BlazorJS). 468+ shared test methods running on both browser and desktop runtimes + libtorrent 2.0 external-interop fixtures.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>BitTorrent;WebTorrent;P2P;Torrent;Blazor;WebAssembly;WebRTC;DHT;Streaming;MachineLearning;ModelDelivery;SIPSorcery</PackageTags>
		<NoPackageAnalysis>true</NoPackageAnalysis>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Demo.Shared" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS" Version="3.5.6" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.AsyncFileSystem" Version="1.2.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS.Cryptography" Version="3.2.0" />
		<!-- SpawnDev.RTC replaces direct SipSorcery dependency - provides cross-platform WebRTC
		     with proven browser-interop SipSorcery fork (SRTP profile fix) bundled inside.
		     PackageReference (not ProjectReference) so CI / GitHub Pages builds work from a
		     standalone SpawnDev.WebTorrent checkout - they don't have the sibling RTC repo.
		     1.1.1 is the minimum version: 1.1.0 declared a dep on public SIPSorcery 10.0.4-pre
		     which doesn't exist on nuget.org; 1.1.1 bundles the fork DLLs inline (ILGPU pattern). -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.RTC" Version="1.1.6" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="windows" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="linux" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="macos" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
